# Phase 3 remoting transport — execution log

- Session: 2026-09-27T06:27:31Z
- Scope: Implement explicit client `start()` lifecycle after prior parity review identified construction-time task startup as a Java lifecycle gap. User clarified Rust API assessment should consider its role in external primary workflows, not merely whether Java has the same name.
- Decisions: constructors remain runtime-independent and validate/configure only; `start()` requires a Tokio runtime, launches inbound/callback/channel-event workers and timeout/NameServer schedulers, and is idempotent. Transport invokes reject pre-start use with `TransportError::NotStarted`; reachability returns false and unknown channels remain writable before start (matching Java's unknown channel behavior). Shutdown before start drops retained worker receivers and prevents restart. No changes to Phase 3 plan files.
- Changes: `crates/rocketmq-classic-remoting/src/client/mod.rs` now stores startup receivers and starts owned tasks on explicit call; transport tests/callers in `tests/transport.rs` and private client unit tests start explicitly. `error.rs` adds `NotStarted`. README, ADR-0001, Known Differences, and Phase 3 inventory describe the lifecycle and public workflow. Added tests for construction without runtime, start requiring runtime and being retryable, pre-start operation rejection, idempotent start, and no restart after shutdown.
- Verification: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --offline` passed (40 unit, 4 codec, 71 transport); `cargo test --workspace --offline` passed; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings` passed; `cargo fmt --all --check` passed; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py` passed; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test` passed; `git diff --check` passed. Focused lifecycle and channel-writability tests passed after the final code change.
- Status: Implementation committed as `2b2edfc feat(remoting): add explicit client start lifecycle`; documentation and this execution log remain uncommitted for a separate documentation commit. Phase 3 acceptance remains open. English/Traditional Chinese plans remain read-only; P3-V04 remains assigned to Phase 19. No Phase 4 work started.
